 ## Background
-The method was introduced as a data-parallel approach for solid voxelization on GPUs [S1]. It was developed to address the inefficiencies of voxel-based parallelization, where every voxel must be tested against the mesh [S2]. The facet-based (FB) approach was shown to be significantly faster than voxel-based (VB) methods due to reduced intersection tests and better memory locality [S2]. It is part of the broader family of GPU and Parallel Acceleration Voxelization techniques [Parent].
+The method was introduced as a data-parallel approach for solid voxelization on GPUs [S1]. It was developed to address the inefficiencies of voxel-based parallelization, where every voxel must be tested against the mesh [S2]. The facet-based (FB) approach was shown to be significantly faster than voxel-based (VB) methods due to reduced intersection tests and better memory locality [S2]. Builds on [GPU and Parallel Acceleration Voxelization](6878-gpu-and-parallel-acceleration-voxelization.md).
 
